Don't bother; at worst, race down there and die
until it goes away. At 2/3rds chance of losing it
per try where it is sucked into the game (also 1
chance in 3, IIRC), you won't need long, and the
games where it isn't selected for inclusion won't be
affected by it.

Meanwhile, take it as a chance to practice never,
ever playing burdened.

You probably won't be any better at that than I am,
but the effort will improve your game.

Note that "surviving gawdawful bones levels" is a
normal part of NetHack and deserves study for better
ways to accomplish it than by burning PCs like
cordwood.

E.g., if you _know_ that M2 Bones is a killer, make
sure a scroll of magic mapping goes with you the
next time you descend to M2, so you can make a
coward's bee-line dash for the down staircase.

If you _know_ a killer warhorse is behind door #2,
don't open _any_ door #2s until you confirm the
level is or isn't that bones file somewhere safer
on the level.

